", allowing only integers; a positive integer sets the number of decimal places, and ",[311,336,337],{},"true"," allows any number. ",[311,340,341],{},"thousand-separator",[311,343,337],{},", showing thousands separators on blur; pass ",[311,346,333],{}," for numbers such as years or codes that should not have them.",[349,350],"component-example",{"name":351},"input-number-decimal",[353,354,355,370,383],"ul",{},[356,357,358,359,362,363,366,367,369],"li",{},"While typing, the sign, decimal point and trailing zeros are kept; incomplete input (such as just ",[311,360,361],{},"-",") binds ",[311,364,365],{},"null",". On blur, the value is rounded and padded according to ",[311,368,329],{},", and thousands separators are shown.",[356,371,372,373,375,376,378,379,382],{},"Non-numeric characters and decimals beyond the set places cannot be typed, and pasted text is reverted too. When ",[311,374,329],{}," is ",[311,377,333],{}," or ",[311,380,381],{},"0",", the decimal point cannot be typed.",[356,384,385,386,375,389,392,393,375,395,378,397,399,400,402],{},"On focus, the text switches to the editable form without separators. ",[311,387,388],{},"inputmode",[311,390,391],{},"numeric"," when ",[311,394,329],{},[311,396,333],{},[311,398,381],{},", and ",[311,401,329],{}," otherwise, so phones show the matching number keyboard.",[321,404,406],{"id":405},"step-buttons","Step buttons",[308,408,409,412,413,416,417,420,421,424,425,428,429,432,433,436,437,440],{},[311,410,411],{},"buttons"," shows increment and decrement buttons (off by default), ",[311,414,415],{},"step"," is the amount per step (",[311,418,419],{},"1"," by default), and ",[311,422,423],{},"min",", ",[311,426,427],{},"max"," limit stepping with the buttons and keys. ",[311,430,431],{},"orientation"," sets the button layout: ",[311,434,435],{},"horizontal"," (default) puts decrement on the left and increment on the right and centers the number; ",[311,438,439],{},"vertical"," stacks both on the right and keeps the number right-aligned.",[349,442],{"name":443},"input-number-step",[353,445,446,469,475,492,508,551,563,570],{},[356,447,448,452,453,455,456,424,458,424,460,462,463,465,466,468],{},[449,450,451],"strong",{},"Keyboard",": with ",[311,454,411],{},", or when any of ",[311,457,415],{},[311,459,423],{},[311,461,427],{}," is passed, ArrowUp \u002F ArrowDown steps once in the focused input, PageUp \u002F PageDown steps 10 times, and Home \u002F End jump to ",[311,464,423],{}," \u002F ",[311,467,427],{}," (when set). Without these settings the arrow keys behave as in a normal text input. The buttons are not in the Tab order and are labelled \"Increment\" and \"Decrement\" (following the locale).",[356,470,471,474],{},[449,472,473],{},"Press and hold",": holding a button for more than 0.4 seconds keeps stepping until a limit is reached or the button is released. Pressing a button does not move focus away from the input.",[356,476,477,480,481,483,484,486,487,489,490,314],{},[449,478,479],{},"Empty value",": when the value is ",[311,482,365],{},", both increment and decrement start at ",[311,485,423],{},", or at ",[311,488,381],{}," without ",[311,491,423],{},[356,493,494,497,498,501,502,505,506,314],{},[449,495,496],{},"No floating-point errors",": steps are computed in decimal, so repeatedly adding ",[311,499,500],{},"0.25"," never gives ",[311,503,504],{},"0.7500000001","; the result is rounded to the places allowed by ",[311,507,329],{},[356,509,510,517,518,520,521,523,524,526,527,529,530,532,533,535,536,538,539,541,542,544,545,547,548,550],{},[449,511,512,514,515],{},[311,513,415],{}," and ",[311,516,329],{},": when ",[311,519,415],{}," has more decimal places than ",[311,522,329],{}," allows (for example ",[311,525,500],{}," with ",[311,528,329],{}," set to ",[311,531,333],{},"), the step is rounded to what ",[311,534,329],{}," allows (at least one smallest unit, ",[311,537,419],{}," for ",[311,540,333],{},") with a console warning. A ",[311,543,415],{}," that is not a number above 0, or a ",[311,546,423],{}," greater than ",[311,549,427],{},", is also ignored with a warning.",[356,552,553,556,557,559,560,562],{},[449,554,555],{},"Limits",": the increment button is disabled when the value is at or above ",[311,558,427],{},", and the decrement button at or below ",[311,561,423],{},". Both are disabled while disabled, loading, in a skeleton or in a disabled form.",[356,564,565,566,569],{},"Each step triggers the ",[311,567,568],{},"UFormField"," input and change validation, just like typing.",[356,571,572,514,574,576,577,314],{},[311,573,411],{},[311,575,431],{}," can have site-wide defaults, for example to show the buttons across the project: ",[311,578,579],{},"shuoUi.components.inputNumber.buttons: true",[581,582,583,514,585,587,588,591,592,514,595,598,599,604],"warning",{},[311,584,423],{},[311,586,427],{}," only limit the buttons and keys. ",[449,589,590],{},"A typed value outside the range is not corrected","; the bound value stays as typed, and stepping from it moves back into the range. Keep validating the range in the schema with ",[311,593,594],{},"v.minValue",[311,596,597],{},"v.maxValue","; see ",[600,601,603],"a",{"href":602},"#with-form-validation","With form validation"," below.",[308,606,607,608,465,611,614,615,618,619,622,623,626],{},"In horizontal layout the decrement button takes the place of the left ",[311,609,610],{},"icon",[311,612,613],{},"leadingIcon"," (the ",[311,616,617],{},"#leading"," slot still follows the button); use ",[311,620,621],{},"orientation=\"vertical\""," when you need a left icon. The increment button sits to the right of the unit, the ",[311,624,625],{},"#trailing"," slot and the loading icon, and the padding on both sides follows their actual width, so the number and unit are never pushed out.",[321,628,630],{"id":629},"unit","Unit",[308,632,633,634,375,636,638,639,642],{},"When ",[311,635,629],{},[311,637,337],{},", \"NTD\" is shown (\"元\" in Traditional Chinese, switching with the locale). The text can be changed in ",[600,640,47],{"href":641},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftheme\u002Fmessages#overridable-items","; passing a string shows that text. Units vary in length, so the right padding follows the unit's actual width and the number never overlaps the unit.",[349,644],{"name":645},"input-number-unit",[308,647,648,514,650,652,653,657,658,660,661,465,663,314],{},[311,649,629],{},[311,651,341],{}," can also have site-wide defaults; see ",[600,654,656],{"href":655},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftheme\u002Fcomponent-defaults#configurable-props","Configurable props",". The site-wide ",[311,659,629],{}," only accepts ",[311,662,337],{},[311,664,333],{},[321,666,668],{"id":667},"variants","Variants",[308,670,671,672,424,675,514,678,681,682,314],{},"Uses the ",[311,673,674],{},"variant",[311,676,677],{},"color",[311,679,680],{},"highlight"," of ",[311,683,684],{},"UInput",[349,686],{"name":687},"input-number-variant",[321,689,690],{"id":610},"Icon",[308,692,671,693,681,695,697],{},[311,694,610],{},[311,696,684],{},", shown on the left alongside the unit.",[349,699],{"name":700},"input-number-icon",[321,702,704],{"id":703},"size-and-states","Size and states",[308,706,707,708,711],{},"While loading, the spinner sits to the right of the unit and the number and unit move left to make room. See ",[600,709,102],{"href":710},"\u002Fcomponents\u002Foverview\u002Fcommon"," for the behavior shared by all states.",[349,713],{"name":714},"input-number-states",[316,716,718],{"id":717},"examples","Examples",[321,720,603],{"id":721},"with-form-validation",[308,723,724,725,728,729,514,731,733,734,737],{},"Use ",[311,726,727],{},"requiredNumber"," for required fields and add ranges with ",[311,730,594],{},[311,732,597],{},"; use ",[311,735,736],{},"optionalNonNegativeNumber"," for optional non-negative numbers. What gets validated and submitted is a number, without separators.",[349,739],{"name":740},"input-number-validation",[321,742,744],{"id":743},"step-buttons-with-validation","Step buttons with validation",[308,746,747,514,749,751],{},[311,748,423],{},[311,750,427],{}," do not replace validation: the buttons in this example only stop at 0, and the schema checks the upper limit; stepping above 40 shows the error right away.",[349,753],{"name":754},"input-number-step-validation",[321,756,758],{"id":757},"centered-numbers","Centered numbers",[308,760,761,764,765,768,769,772,773,775,776,778],{},[311,762,763],{},"ui.base"," has a built-in ",[311,766,767],{},"text-right","; pass ",[311,770,771],{},"text-center"," to center the number, which suits short fields inside a sentence. With horizontal step buttons the built-in value is ",[311,774,771],{},", so the number sits between the buttons; pass ",[311,777,767],{}," to keep it right-aligned. With a unit or while loading, the right padding follows the trailing content's actual width, so the number never overlaps the unit.",[349,780],{"name":781},"input-number-center",[321,783,785],{"id":784},"clear-button","Clear button",[308,787,788,789,791,792,794,795,604],{},"Put a clear button in ",[311,790,625],{},". ",[311,793,625],{}," sits next to the unit and the loading icon without replacing them; see ",[600,796,798],{"href":797},"#slots","Slots",[349,800],{"name":801},"input-number-clearable",[321,803,805],{"id":804},"accessing-the-native-input","Accessing the native input",[308,807,808,809,812],{},"Get the native input through ",[311,810,811],{},"inputRef"," on the template ref.",[349,814],{"name":815},"input-number-expose",[316,817,819],{"id":818},"props","Props",[821,822],"component-props",{"name":823},"ShuoInputNumber",[308,825,826,827,830,831,424,834,424,837,424,840,424,843,514,846,314],{},"See ",[600,828,102],{"href":829},"\u002Fcomponents\u002Foverview\u002Fcommon#shared-props"," for the behavior of ",[311,832,833],{},"size",[311,835,836],{},"disabled",[311,838,839],{},"loading",[311,841,842],{},"skeleton",[311,844,845],{},"id",[311,847,848],{},"name",[316,850,798],{"id":851},"slots",[853,85